---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Who's behind J Curato Solutions, and why this blog exists."
	pubDate={new Date('2026-08-30')}
>
	<p>
		I'm John, a DevOps engineer based in Chennai. J Curato Solutions is the consulting and
		training venture I run alongside that work — this blog is its content arm.
	</p>

	<p>
		Most DevOps content online falls into two buckets: tutorials that stop the moment a cluster
		actually breaks, and reference docs that assume you already know what's wrong. Neither one
		helps when a developer walks over and asks why a pod that clearly "completed" left no trace of
		what it did.
	</p>

	<p>
		Every post here starts from a real incident — something that broke, the wrong assumption I
		made first, and the mechanical reason underneath it once I stopped guessing. If a post doesn't
		have a genuine failure behind it, it doesn't get written.
	</p>

	<p>
		This blog is also where the material for a DevOps + AI training cohort is coming from.
		Content and course material are being built together, not one after the other — so what you
		read here is the same thing a future cohort would work through, not a marketing version of it.
	</p>

	<p>
		If that's useful to you, <a href="/blog">start with the blog</a>, or <a
			href="mailto:jcuratosolutions@gmail.com?subject=Notify%20me%20about%20the%20DevOps%20%2B%20AI%20cohort"
			>get in touch</a
		> about the cohort.
	</p>
</Layout>
